From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:44:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Thief: the haze lit by every lamp, half its cells a frame

With the fog's all-lights estimate on (and nothing on the raster side
reading the volume), every one of the grid's 900k cells picked a light and
traced a shadow ray every frame: 5 ms of a frame at Reflections in Red's
pond. A cell wholly behind what is seen (depth gate 0: its light is
multiplied by 0) now carries its reprojected history forward instead, as
does every other slice of the grid's depth each frame (alternating; whole
slices, so a threadgroup skips together -- a checkerboard saved nothing);
a fresh sample is blended in at 0.08 instead of 0.05, for about the same
responsiveness. Smoke puffs and a volume the raster reads are as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0137FfF2kXgpYFjmGxKqakLV
---
 Source/Shaders/RtVolumetric.comp | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Shaders/RtVolumetric.comp b/Source/Shaders/RtVolumetric.comp
index 6dc8b91..9bf0ab7 100644
--- a/Source/Shaders/RtVolumetric.comp
+++ b/Source/Shaders/RtVolumetric.comp
@@ -544,6 +544,31 @@ void main()
             radiance_Prev = vec3( 0 );
         }
 
+        // Thief RT: the haze lit by every lamp (the fog's all-lights estimate, nothing on
+        // the raster side reading the volume) costs a light pick and a shadow ray in each
+        // of the grid's 900k cells, every frame -- 5 ms of a frame at Reflections in Red's
+        // pond. Two cuts, both carrying the cell's (reprojected) history forward instead:
+        //  - a cell wholly behind what is seen (depth gate 0): its light is multiplied
+        //    by 0 anyway (the single-light path already skips these);
+        //  - the rest, half of them a frame (every other slice of the grid's depth,
+        //    alternating): its history is 95% of it already, so a fresh sample every
+        //    other frame, blended in at a little more, keeps nearly the same look.
+        //    (Whole slices, not a checkerboard: the cells of a threadgroup run together,
+        //    and with half of each skipping the group took as long as before.)
+        // Smoke puffs and a volume the raster reads (illumVolumeEnable) are as before.
+        const bool fogOnly    = globalUniform.illumVolumeEnable == 0 && !inSmoke &&
+                                globalUniform.volumeShaftDebug == 0;
+        const bool behind     = fogOnly && depthGate <= 0.0;
+        const bool otherFrame = fogOnly && histValid &&
+                                ( ( uint( cell.z ) + globalUniform.frameId ) & 1u ) != 0;
+        vec3 tolight = vec3( 0, 1, 0 );
+        if( behind || otherFrame )
+        {
+            radiance = radiance_Prev;
+        }
+        else
+        {
+
         uint seed =
             getRandomSeed( ivec2( cell.x + cell.z, cell.y + 19 * cell.z ), globalUniform.frameId );
 
@@ -562,8 +587,6 @@ void main()
             s.toViewerDir     = toviewer;
         }
 
-        vec3 tolight = vec3( 0, 1, 0 );
-
         // MULTIPLE SAMPLES, but only where there is smoke.
         //
         // Everything else added for the noise -- the spatial filter, the
@@ -635,7 +658,8 @@ void main()
                             : inSmoke  ? globalUniform.smokeIllumBlend
                                        : 0.05;
 
-        radiance = mix( radiance_Prev, radiance, blend );
+        radiance = mix( radiance_Prev, radiance, fogOnly && histValid ? 0.08 : blend );
+        }
 
         lighting += globalUniform.volumeLightMult * radiance *
                     phaseFunction_Schlick( tolight, toviewer, globalUniform.volumeAsymmetry );
